# NFS Exports Configuration
# This file defines what directories are exported via NFS
# Format: <directory> <host>(<options>)

# Main export directory for SeaweedFS and other services
# Allows read-write access to all clients in the network
/nfs-share  *(rw,async,no_subtree_check,no_root_squash,fsid=0)

# Alternative: Restrict to specific network (more secure)
# /nfs-share  172.30.0.0/16(rw,async,no_subtree_check,no_root_squash,fsid=0)

# Note:
# - rw: read-write access
# - async: server acks writes before disk commit — avoids stalls under large
#   (multi-hundred-MB checkpoint) write bursts. Trade-off: on power loss, writes
#   acked-but-not-flushed can be lost. Acceptable here: /nfs-share holds SeaweedFS
#   volumes + /aiml/tmp scratch (model checkpoints), all reproducible. Switch back
#   to `sync` if this export ever holds data that must survive a hard crash.
# - no_subtree_check: improves performance
# - no_root_squash: allows root access (needed for Docker containers)
# - fsid=0: required for NFSv4 root export
